# night-veil-ubuntu Tor configuration (roadmap step 5.3a).
#
# SOCKS on loopback only: the Warden's Waggle transport (and nothing else -- no other process on
# this Cell has a reason to proxy through Tor directly) dials 127.0.0.1:9050 to reach the Hive
# Stand's own hidden service (codingrules section 8.7: "the Waggle client's socket routed through
# the Tor SOCKS proxy, not the VPN interface").
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050

# The control port, cookie-authenticated (no password on disk to leak): used by
# hivemind.hive.night_veil.session_commands' own hidden_service_cmd and, in a later phase, by
# anything that needs Tor's own circuit status rather than a plain SOCKS request.
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
CookieAuthentication 1

# No logs retained (codingrules section 12: "the Cell's local trail detail and its logs" are part
# of the Night Veil boundary that never survives teardown -- Tor's own log is one of the "side
# channels" ADR-0030 names). /dev/null, not a rotated file: nothing here to leak even mid-session.
Log notice file /dev/null

DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
User debian-tor

# Never advertise this Cell as a relay or bridge: it is a Tor *client* only.
ClientOnly 1
